//! Cases for `Number`, `Math`, `parseInt`, `parseFloat`,
//! `StringToNumber` and the global value properties (M7 feature 4). The
//! expected output of each case is the output of Node.js 22 for the same
//! script (`print` joins `String` of its arguments), generated by a
//! Node.js script; the cases of `Math.sumPrecise` and `Math.f16round`,
//! which Node.js 22 does not have, were measured in Chromium 148; the
//! digits of `toString(radix)` in radixes other than 10 come from the
//! `BigInt` reference of swb's definition
//! (`js-text/tests/data/radix-reference.js`, ADR 0026 section 15), which
//! differs from Node.js in the last digits of some values. Each case also
//! runs in the GC stress mode.

#![allow(clippy::too_many_lines, reason = "a test is a list of script cases")]

mod common;

use common::check_cases;

